  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThere is a difference between browsers if a `dialog[popover]` is focusable by default (no tabindex specified).\n\n- Chromium: the `<dialog>` is not focusable/tabstop by default\n- FF & WebKit: the `<dialog>` *is* a focusable/tabstop by default\n\nhttps://codepen.io/jpzwarte/pen/jErdrGm?editors=1100\n\n1. Click the \"open dialog[popover]\"\n2. Press SHIFT if focus isn't already clear by the hotpink border\n3. Focus should be on the `<button>` inside the dialog\n4. Press SHIFT-TAB\n\nIn Chrome, focus is on the original button that opened the popover. In the other browsers, the dialog itself has focus.\n\nWhich is correct? Is this an ambiguity in the spec maybe?",
